  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Psychology A.A. Degree - Local GE' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published September 15, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7499/PublishedPdf). GE Pattern: SCC Local GE. Official Total Units: 60-62; this seed models the first-listed/recommended low path = 15 + 15 + 15 + 15 = 60 units (ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page; PSYC 330 at 3 units). Semester sums verified against the map's 15-16 / 15-16 / 15 / 15 headers. 4 terms (within the AA/AS 4-7 gate). Distinct from map 7760 (sacramento-city-college-aa-psychology), which is the Cal-GETC GE version of the same program. Major Elective slots: (1) Sem 1: PSYC 316 / 320 / 370 / EDUC 300 — PSYC 316 selected (first-listed, 3 units); PSYC 370 is the recommended course for students transferring to CSU Sacramento (per map note). (2) Sem 2: minimum 3 units from PSYC 314, PSYC 315, PSYC 340+, PSYC 356, PSYC 358, PSYC 360, PSYC 364, PSYC 367, PSYC 374/GERON 302, PSYC 390, PSYC 405/ADMJ 303 (also PSYC 316, PSYC 370, or EDUC 300 if not already used) — PSYC 314 selected (first-listed, 3 units). Prerequisites documented: PSYC 310 requires PSYC C1000 with 'C' or better; PSYC 335 requires PSYC C1000 and (PSYC 330 or STAT C1000 or STAT C1000H) with 'C' or better; PSYC 340 requires PSYC C1000 with 'C' or better. Choice slots: (1) GE ENGL C1000 / ENGL 488 / ESLW 340, SCC Local Area L1A — ENGL C1000 selected (3 units); (2) GE INDIS 313 / HCD 310, Life Development Skills, SCC Local Area L7B — INDIS 313 selected (first-listed; first-time FYE students take INDIS 313); (3) ME PSYC 330 / STAT C1000 / STAT C1000H, Introductory Statistics for the Behavioral Sciences, SCC Local Area L2 — PSYC 330 selected (first-listed, 3 units; faculty-recommended for CSU Sacramento transfer; students with STAT C1000 placement may take PSYC 330 instead). Students not placing directly in ENGL C1000 take the ENGL 80/ENGL C1000 combo; ENGL 488 requires ESL 325 with 'C' or better or placement; ESLW 340 requires ESL 325 with 'C' or better or Los Rios assessment placement. Students not placing directly in STAT C1000 take STAT 10/PSYC 330 or STAT 10/STAT C1000 combo (STAT 10/PSYC 330 combo only offered Spring). PSYC C1000 fills SCC Local Area L4. Electives: any courses numbered 100-499 (see a counselor). AA/AS requirements: 60 degree-applicable units with 2.0 GPA, 12 units within Los Rios, each required course 'C' or better, SCC Local GE Areas L1A-L7B. Bachelor's-degree holders are deemed to have satisfied GE (per map). Psychology, People & Society Meta Majors.",
